{
  "_doc": [
    "THE K->0 DELETION LEDGER for the `condition:` compatibility field, read by",
    "scripts/test-route-reachability.js. Not a hiding place — a countdown that can only run down.",
    "",
    "WHAT A ROW MEANS: this legacy condition token is emitted by production today and is read by",
    "NOTHING outside production — not by any of the six routing surfaces, not by a contract",
    "validator, not by a `scripts/test-*` / `simulate-*` suite, and not by a doc or role profile.",
    "`condition:` is migration staging, so a row here is a field scheduled for deletion, not a",
    "compatibility promise being kept. Every consumer of these tokens is ours; there is no third",
    "party to break.",
    "",
    "HOW THE RATCHET WORKS:",
    "  1. Enforcement is DEFAULT-ON and EXEMPT-BY-BASELINE, never an opt-in allowlist. A token",
    "     that is NOT listed here and has no consumer FAILS THE BUILD, naming the file and line",
    "     that emits it. A newly minted legacy token is loud on arrival.",
    "  2. The list may only SHRINK. Deleting a row (because the token was deleted, or gained a",
    "     real consumer) is the only maintenance path. Adding a row is not a fix, and the suite",
    "     will not let one hide: an entry whose token has acquired a consumer, or is no longer",
    "     emitted anywhere, FAILS as stale and demands its own deletion. Both directions are red.",
    "  3. Entries are sorted and unique, and the suite asserts both — an unsorted append-only",
    "     ledger merges dirty, and a clean merge that silently drops work is a failure mode this",
    "     campaign has already paid for once.",
    "",
    "THE REASON IS PER-LEDGER, NOT PER-ROW, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE. The exempt-list convention",
    "asks for a one-line reason per entry; 284 hand-written reasons would say the same sentence",
    "284 times and would be noise, not evidence. The single reason is: these are the pre-existing",
    "K measured when the trigger was built, and the trigger exists to drive this list to empty.",
    "A row added AFTER that seeding is a different act and should be argued for in its commit.",
    "",
    "Regenerate the measurement (reports only, never writes):",
    "  node scripts/test-route-reachability.js --condition-census",
    "",
    "Seeded 2026-07-28 against distinct_condition_values=737, of which 284 had no consumer.",
    "Owner: the ADR 0013 M3 refusal-census campaign. Target: this array is empty and K is 0."
  ],
